#
# F9 negative fixture: a manifest that DECLARES a test in its `mf:entries` list
# but never DESCRIBES it (no `rdf:type`/`mf:name`/`mf:action` triples at all) —
# the exact silent-skip shape `crate::manifest::load`'s completeness check
# exists to catch (see its doc comment in `crates/sparql-conformance/src/
# manifest.rs`, around the `list_entry_iris`/`missing` logic).
#
# Deliberately placed OUTSIDE `suite/`: `crates/sparql-conformance/tests/
# sparql_conformance.rs`'s `datatest_stable::harness!` only discovers
# `suite/**/manifest.ttl`, so this file is never picked up as a live
# conformance case — it exists ONLY to be fed to `manifest::load` directly by
# `crates/sparql-conformance/tests/suite_inventory.rs`'s
# `broken_manifest_with_an_undescribed_entry_is_rejected` test, proving the
# guard actually fires rather than merely existing unexercised.
@prefix mf: <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#> .

<#manifest> a mf:Manifest ;
    mf:entries ( <#undescribedEntry> ) .

# <#undescribedEntry> is a member of the mf:entries list above but carries NO
# rdf:type, mf:name, or mf:action triples anywhere in this document — the
# loader's row-grouping SELECT requires all three to bind, so this entry
# produces no row and would otherwise vanish from the loaded case set with no
# trace.
